                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "36244802",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198099919200",
                            "num_reviews": 2,
                            "playtime_forever": 811,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 811,
                            "last_played": 1509722854
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I can play as the Great Old Ones instead of Investigators, how cool is that! \n\nAbout the theme:\nCompare to other Cthulhu game, this one is more like a hardcore board game or a strategy game. Maybe this reverse setting is also the reason why this game has less horror and darkness, more killing and deploy forces.\n\nGameplay:\nThe skills of Deities, servants and investigators are stunning. In chapter 2, each level has 2 different investigator skills, which made me have to change talent skills every time I enter a new level, and develop different combinations. It’s kind of hard, but also brainy and fun.\nFor beginners and gamers don’t know Cthulhu Mythos, it may be hard to understand SAN and Threat. And there also are many hidden rules that you can only discover in the game. It is interesting for senior players, but a background introduction or a more detailed tutorial may be friendlier for novices.\n\nOperation:\nThis game looks simple but actually has very complex contents. I believe there is still space for improvement for the operation of moving servants. It’s kind of dizzy to move servants to a spot on the other side of the map.\n\nI recommend this game for its delicate Deity, Servant and Investigator skill design, it is definitely a great choice for people who like challenge. \n",
